# Routes and auth

## App Router groups

```text
src/app/
  layout.tsx           # root: fonts, providers
  (auth)/              # login — no MainShell
  (app)/               # authenticated — AuthGuard + MainShell
    layout.tsx
    <feature>/page.tsx
```

- **Guards** in layout: `AuthGuard`, role/route guards (`PostAuthRouteGuard`), not in every page.

## Route path constants (recommended)

Create **`src/lib/route-paths.ts`**:

```typescript
export const RoutePaths = {
  home: "/dashboard",
  fleet: "/fleet",
  driverPortal: "/driver",
  driverHistory: "/driver/history",
} as const;
```

Use in `Link href`, `router.push`, and nav config — **no duplicated path strings**.

## Dynamic routes

- Next 15+: `params: Promise<{ id: string }>` and `await params` in server pages.
- Prefer **client pages** when the whole feature needs Bearer token + Query (current myth-delivery pattern).

## Post-login routing

- Centralize **`getPostLoginRoute(roles)`** in lib — controllers call after login success.

## Deep linking / RBAC

- Hide nav items with role hooks (`useIsAdmin`, `useCanFleetOperations`, …).
- **Also** enforce on API (backend); UI hiding is not security.

## Optional: feature registry

For large products, `src/config/features.ts` can list modules (id, title, href) for docs or placeholder nav — not required for CRUD apps.
